        "title": "Log End Offset (LEO) vs High-Water Mark (HWM) Boundaries",
        "say": [
          "In a distributed streaming cluster, partitions are replicated across multiple broker nodes to ensure fault tolerance. Code reviews for changes in this area should focus on correctness and clarity rather than style preferences, because a subtle logic error here can have outsized impact on the entire system.",
          "One broker acts as the partition leader handling all client writes, while follower brokers asynchronously replicate the log. Pair programming sessions on complex implementations of this pattern produce better designs because two engineers catch different categories of mistakes and bring complementary domain knowledge.",
          "This replication architecture creates two critical offset coordinates within every partition: Log End Offset and High-Water Mark. Writing a design document before implementing a significant change to this component creates a shared understanding among team members and surfaces objections early when they are cheapest to address.",
          "The Log End Offset, or LEO, is the offset of the very next record to be written to the leader's local partition log. Onboarding new team members should include a walkthrough of this component with concrete examples of recent bugs and how they were diagnosed, giving newcomers actionable mental models for debugging.",
          "The High-Water Mark, or HWM, is the highest offset that has been successfully replicated across all in-sync follower replicas (ISR). Retrospectives that examine how well the team applied this principle in the last sprint identify process improvements that compound over time into significantly higher engineering velocity.",
          "Records between the High-Water Mark and the Log End Offset are physically present on the leader, but have not yet been fully replicated. Shared ownership of this component, where any team member can confidently make changes, requires comprehensive tests, clear documentation, and regular knowledge-sharing sessions that build collective expertise.",
          "To prevent dirty reads and phantom data loss during broker failovers, consumers are strictly forbidden from reading past the High-Water Mark. Defining an on-call runbook for this component that covers the five most common failure modes and their remediation steps reduces mean time to recovery and lowers on-call stress significantly.",
          "If a consumer read uncommitted records and the leader crashed before replication finished, the new leader would not have those records. Cross-team dependencies on this component should be managed through versioned interfaces and change notifications so that upstream changes do not silently break downstream consumers or introduce regressions.",
          "The High-Water Mark boundary guarantees read isolation, ensuring consumers only ever observe fully replicated and durable events. Celebrating when the team catches a potential issue in this area during code review reinforces the culture of careful engineering and encourages thorough reviews in future pull requests."
        ],
        "example": "A real estate contract signed by the seller (LEO) which is not legally binding until the buyer's escrow funds clear and the deed is stamped at city hall (HWM).",
        "code": "interface PartitionWatermarkState {\n  leaderLEO: number;\n  followerLEOs: Map<string, number>;\n  highWaterMark: number;\n}\n\nclass WatermarkCoordinator {\n  private leaderLEO: number = 0;\n  private followerLEOs: Map<string, number> = new Map([\n    ['broker-2', 0],\n    ['broker-3', 0]\n  ]);\n\n  writeLeader(messageCount: number): void {\n    this.leaderLEO += messageCount;\n  }\n\n  replicateFollower(followerId: string, ackOffset: number): void {\n    this.followerLEOs.set(followerId, ackOffset);\n  }\n\n  computeHighWaterMark(): number {\n    const allOffsets = [this.leaderLEO, ...Array.from(this.followerLEOs.values())];\n    return Math.min(...allOffsets);\n  }\n\n  getState(): PartitionWatermarkState {\n    return {\n      leaderLEO: this.leaderLEO,\n      followerLEOs: new Map(this.followerLEOs),\n      highWaterMark: this.computeHighWaterMark()\n    };\n  }\n}\n\nconst coord = new WatermarkCoordinator();\ncoord.writeLeader(5);\nconsole.log('Leader wrote 5 messages. LEO=5. Initial HWM:', coord.computeHighWaterMark());\n\ncoord.replicateFollower('broker-2', 5);\ncoord.replicateFollower('broker-3', 3);\nconsole.log('Follower 2 at 5, Follower 3 at 3. Updated HWM:', coord.computeHighWaterMark());\n\ncoord.replicateFollower('broker-3', 5);\nconsole.log('All followers caught up. Final HWM:', coord.computeHighWaterMark());",
        "output": "Leader wrote 5 messages. LEO=5. Initial HWM: 0\nFollower 2 at 5, Follower 3 at 3. Updated HWM: 3\nAll followers caught up. Final HWM: 5",
