          "In modern microservice architectures, a single consumer process can rarely keep pace with high-velocity producer event streams. Defining an on-call runbook for this component that covers the five most common failure modes and their remediation steps reduces mean time to recovery and lowers on-call stress significantly. Cross-team dependencies on this component should be managed through versioned interfaces and change notifications so that upstream changes do not silently break downstream consumers or introduce regressions.",
