          "In distributed systems, the physics of unreliable networks and independent failure modes force systems to make architectural trade-offs. Automated tests for this kind of logic should cover not just the happy path but also boundary conditions, error handling, and concurrent access scenarios that are common in production. Monitoring and observability are essential companions to this technique because they let you verify at runtime that the system is behaving as designed rather than relying on hope.",
          "Every event streaming architecture falls into one of three distinct delivery semantic classifications. Code that implements this pattern should be isolated behind a clean interface so that future improvements or replacements do not require changes throughout the entire codebase.",
