          "In naive software designs, engineers frequently buffer incoming events in standard memory arrays or unbounded queues. Defining an on-call runbook for this component that covers the five most common failure modes and their remediation steps reduces mean time to recovery and lowers on-call stress significantly. Cross-team dependencies on this component should be managed through versioned interfaces and change notifications so that upstream changes do not silently break downstream consumers or introduce regressions.",
          "Under normal traffic conditions where consumption rate exceeds ingestion rate, the queue stays nearly empty and appears to function perfectly. Celebrating when the team catches a potential issue in this area during code review reinforces the culture of careful engineering and encourages thorough reviews in future pull requests.",
