          "In Node.js and TypeScript runtimes, the V8 JavaScript engine enforces a strict heap limit, typically around two to four gigabytes. The intuition behind this idea extends far beyond textbook examples because production systems combine multiple interacting components that amplify small inefficiencies into serious bottlenecks.",
          "As the unbounded queue expands, V8 garbage collection spends increasing CPU cycles attempting to reclaim memory, causing catastrophic stop-the-world GC pauses. Developing a solid mental model of how this works at a low level allows you to debug problems faster and propose better architectural solutions during system design discussions.",
