          "In production operations, streaming engineers track telemetry to verify that micro-batching is functioning effectively. Technical debt in this component should be tracked explicitly and prioritised alongside feature work, because deferred maintenance eventually manifests as production incidents or development slowdowns that cost more. Understanding this concept thoroughly helps you reason about why certain design choices outperform others in real-world production environments where reliability and speed both matter.",
          "The primary metric evaluating batching quality is Batch Packing Density: the average number of records contained in each dispatched batch. When you grasp the underlying mechanics, you can predict how the system will behave under unusual conditions such as sudden traffic spikes or partial hardware failures.",
          "If a high-throughput topic reports an average packing density of 1.1 records per batch, micro-batching is broken or linger.ms is set to zero. The intuition behind this idea extends far beyond textbook examples because production systems combine multiple interacting components that amplify small inefficiencies into serious bottlenecks.",
