          "Conversely, an average packing density of fifty to two hundred records per batch indicates healthy, efficient micro-batching. Many experienced engineers consider this foundational knowledge because it appears in some form across almost every large-scale system built in the last decade.",
          "Engineers also track TCP packet efficiency: the ratio of payload bytes to total wire bytes transmitted over the network interface. The practical value of mastering this topic becomes apparent during code reviews and architecture meetings where you must justify design tradeoffs with concrete reasoning.",
          "By adjusting linger.ms from zero to five milliseconds, organizations routinely observe a four-fold increase in packing density. Once you internalise the core principle, you will notice its influence in frameworks, libraries, and platform services that abstract it away behind simpler interfaces.",
