          "If the Node.js application sets its concurrency ceiling to fifty, the service will only achieve two hundred and fifty payments per second, failing SLA! Common pitfalls include off-by-one errors in boundary conditions, race conditions in concurrent access paths, and silent data corruption that only manifests long after the initial bug was introduced.",
          "Conversely, if the application opens two thousand concurrent connections, it may overwhelm the external bank API and trigger rate-limiting errors. Structured logging with consistent field names and severity levels allows you to filter millions of log entries down to the handful that are relevant to the incident under investigation.",
          "By calculating the exact concurrency target dictated by Little's Law, engineers configure optimal connection pools and bounded worker pools. Post-incident reviews should identify not just the immediate cause but also the contributing factors such as missing tests, inadequate monitoring, or unclear documentation that allowed the issue.",
