          "Operations alerts fire if queue saturation remains above seventy percent for more than thirty seconds. This knowledge transfers directly into adjacent domains, making it one of the highest-leverage concepts you can invest time in learning early in your career. In practice, teams that apply this correctly report fewer production incidents and faster recovery times because the operational runbook becomes straightforward and well-documented.",
          "The third metric is 95th Percentile (p95) Latency, measuring elapsed time from producer enqueue to batch dispatch. A common mistake beginners make is skipping the planning phase and jumping directly to implementation, which often leads to rework when edge cases surface during testing.",
          "The telemetry engine maintains a sliding histogram of recent latency samples to compute accurate percentiles. Production experience shows that the simplest correct approach usually wins over a clever but fragile optimization, because simplicity makes debugging, testing, and onboarding easier.",
