          "While local state stores provide ultra-low latency, storing state exclusively on local worker disks introduces an existential hazard. Once you internalise the core principle, you will notice its influence in frameworks, libraries, and platform services that abstract it away behind simpler interfaces. Real interview questions at top companies frequently test whether candidates understand the nuances of this topic rather than just the surface-level definition.",
          "What happens when the physical machine hosting the stream worker experiences hardware failure or sudden power loss? Professional developers who understand this deeply can anticipate failure modes before they happen, reducing costly production incidents and improving overall system uptime.",
          "If state only exists in local RAM or an unbacked local SSD, the entire state history is permanently destroyed. This knowledge transfers directly into adjacent domains, making it one of the highest-leverage concepts you can invest time in learning early in your career.",
