          "In production stream processors, balancing fast read latency with durable changelog persistence requires write-through design. Code that implements this pattern should be isolated behind a clean interface so that future improvements or replacements do not require changes throughout the entire codebase. Documentation of the design rationale is just as important as the code itself because future team members need to understand why this approach was chosen over alternatives.",
