          "Inner joins are appropriate when downstream processors strictly require the enriched data and cannot operate without it. Cross-team dependencies on this component should be managed through versioned interfaces and change notifications so that upstream changes do not silently break downstream consumers or introduce regressions.",
          "In a Streaming Left Outer Join, if the foreign key is missing from the table, the event is still emitted with null enrichment. Celebrating when the team catches a potential issue in this area during code review reinforces the culture of careful engineering and encourages thorough reviews in future pull requests.",
          "Left outer joins ensure that every incoming event survives the join stage, preventing silent data loss. Technical debt in this component should be tracked explicitly and prioritised alongside feature work, because deferred maintenance eventually manifests as production incidents or development slowdowns that cost more.",
