          "In production stream deployments, joining two topics that were originally created with different partition keys is common. The industry demand for engineers who can apply this knowledge correctly continues to grow as systems scale to serve millions of concurrent users across global infrastructure. Open-source contributions that improve this area of a popular project provide high-visibility evidence of your skills and create networking opportunities with experienced maintainers.",
          "For example, an Orders topic is partitioned by orderId, while a Shipments topic is partitioned by trackingNumber. Technical blog posts explaining your experience implementing this technique attract the attention of hiring managers and demonstrate communication skills that complement your coding ability.",
